At Thu, 9 Nov 2006 15:22:34 +0530,
aditya shankar wrote:
> 
> Takashi-san,
>  
> We tried invoking an IOCTL on /dev/mixer with command SOUND_MIXER_WRITE_RECSRC. It did
> not seem to invoke the put function of the kcontrol for selecting recording source
> (it's "Master Input Capture").

"Master Input Capture" is an uncommon name, and it won't be mapped to
OSS mixer elements unless you specify via proc file.


> Also, can I add my own IOCTL commands and route control to their implementations?

No for oss mixer API.  Yes for ALSA native API using hwdep device.


Takashi


